<title>ITALY: Italy's Turin sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Turin sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Turin said its June consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 1.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In May, Turin's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Turin is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Friday and Monday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 8.81 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1    (0.2)    1.7  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.1    (0.2)   -0.4  (0.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2    (0.1)    4.3  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0    (0.0)    5.9  (5.8)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.4)    1.3  (1.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1    (0.0)    1.9  (1.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.1    (0.1)    1.3  (1.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.2    (0.0)   -1.0 (-0.8)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.6)    1.0  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1    (0.1)    0.7  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2    (1.6)    4.1  (3.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
